<title>CHILE: Chile's Enap, Cordex sign oil deal.</title>
<headline>Chile's Enap, Cordex sign oil deal.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian energy company Cordex Petroleums Inc signed Tuesday a deal with Chile's state oil company Empresa Nacional del Petroleo (Enap) to explore for oil and natural gas in Chile's far south.</p>
<p>Under the pact, Cordex will invest up to $15 million in three phases over the next 10 years in an area known as Bloque Fell near the port of Punta Arenas.</p>
<p>&quot;There area has obvious production potential given the vicinity of known hydro-carbon fields,&quot; said Dan Gish, executive vice president of Cordex.</p>
</text>
